H_PROVIDER_VERSION` env var selects v1 vs v2 provider (different token-tokens API paths: `/api/auth/tokens` vs `/api/v1/auth/tokens`).\n- All data-API calls now go through `cli.NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` or `auth.TokenForResource` — `LookupCurrentToken` is reserved strictly for auth-host commands. Dispatch's CloudClient and the search service client were updated accordingly.\n- Friendlier errors when auth host returns HTML instead of JSON.\n- Legacy keyring fallback to migrate existing users (`ErrMalformed` → re-fetch path).\n\n**Documentation added:**\n\n- `auth/README.md` — full design rationale, embedding checklist, non-goals.\n- New CLAUDE.md section \"Auth and token resolution\" documenting the contract for callers (always go through `tokenmanager.Manager.Token`, never read keyring directly for data APIs).\n\n**Test additions:** ~2,200 lines of new tests across `deviceflow`, `sts`, `tokens`, `tokenstore`, `tokenmanager`, plus shim-level tests for provider, exchange, store, client. Recent commits include \"round-2 review fixes\" and \"PR review fixes (parallel-safe clock pin, struct cache key)\" — review-driven hardening is already in flight.\n\n**Out of scope (verified clean):** No frontend, no protocol, no strategy, no checkpoint changes. Only commit/dispatch wiring touches the rest of the CLI, and only to route through the new entry points.\n\nI'll send the reviewers' findings as a follow-up when they return."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4163,"cache_read_input_tokens":77818,"output_tokens":1268,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4163,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1268,"cache_read_input_tokens":77818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_i