{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-05-08T11:05:52.965Z","sessionId":"49549d0b-166a-48f3-a7cd-2a93ea53dbe7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aebdb16b685d2eccb</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-soph-Work-entire-devenv-cli-experiments/49549d0b-166a-48f3-a7cd-2a93ea53dbe7/tasks/aebdb16b685d2eccb.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Architecture review of auth split\" completed</summary>\n<result>I have the full picture. Let me draft the architecture review.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Review: `alex/cli-auth-consolidation`\n\n### 1. Architecture Overview\n\nThe branch cleanly separates a reusable OAuth library (`auth/`) from an entire-specific shim (`cmd/entire/cli/auth/`). Library has 5 subpackages plus `internal/oauthhttp`; the shim adds provider tables, env-var reads, keyring service name, legacy bare-string fallback, and singleton wiring. Data-API call sites flow through `cli.NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` (`cmd/entire/cli/api_client.go:36`) or `auth.TokenForResource` (`cmd/entire/cli/auth/exchange.go:74`).\n\n### 2. Compliance Check\n\n**Library purity (good).** `grep` for env-var reads under `auth/` returns nothing. `auth/doc.go:13-16` and `auth/README.md:5,98-102` explicitly forbid globals/env vars/implicit URLs, and the code matches the stated contract. `tokenmanager.Config` (`auth/tokenmanager/tokenmanager.go:55-97`) takes every wire-affecting value as a field. `sts.Client` (`auth/sts/sts.go:76-80`) and `deviceflow.Client` are field-bag structs — no provider table inside the library.\n\n**Single entry-point invariant (mostly held).** Every data-API caller (`activity_cmd.go`, `dispatch_wizard.go`, `trail_cmd.go`, `recap.go`, `search_cmd.go:229`) goes through `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient`. The dispatch cloud path (`mode_cloud.go:35`) routes through `lookupResourceToken` → `auth.TokenForResource`, and search (`search_cmd.go:116`) does the same. `api/client.go:57` adds `errEmptyBearerToken` as a runtime tripwire if a caller bypasses construction. This is a strong invariant — well done.\n\n**Keyring isolation.** No direct `keyring.*` calls outside `auth/tokenstore/` and the shim's two backward-compat fallback reads (`store.go:80,121`).\n\n### 3. Findings (ranked)\n\n#### High — `api/auth_tokens.go` duplicates the provider env var, breaking the single-source-of-truth claim\n`cmd/entire/cli/api/auth_tokens.go:32-42` reads `ENTIRE_AUTH_PROVIDER_VERSION` directly to switch between `/api/v1/auth/tokens` and `/api/auth/tokens`, with a comment explaining the duplication is to avoid an `api → auth` import. The provider table in `cmd/entire/cli/auth/provider.go:35-47` already encodes per-version paths (`deviceCodePath`, `tokenPath`, `stsPath`); auth-tokens path belongs in the same struct. Fix: add `authTokensPath` to `providerConfig`, then either (a) inject it into the `api.Client` at construction, or (b) move `authTokensBasePath()` into the auth shim and call it via a small accessor. As written, two files independently parse the same env var — exactly the leak the comment is apologizing for.\n\n#### High — Provider switch is on `os.Getenv` at call time, not on construction\n`currentProvider()` (`provider.go:53-60`) reads `ENTIRE_AUTH_PROVIDER_VERSION` every time it's called. `defaultManager()` (`exchange.go:48-68`) freezes via `sync.Once`, but `NewClient` (`client.go:47-58`) does not — login can pick v2 while a later in-process call (e.g. via `auth.TokenForResource`) sees a v1 manager if env was changed. Real risk in long-running processes / tests. Also the comment at `exchange.go:46-47` admits \"later env-var changes within the same process are ignored\" — that's surprising-by-design. Fix: read env once at startup into a typed `Provider` value and pass it explicitly into `NewClient`/`defaultManager`.\n\n#### Medium — `LookupCurrentToken` is a public name that invites misuse\n`store.go:140-142` returns the auth-host bearer. CLAUDE.md (`cmd/entire/cli/cli_experiments/CLAUDE.md` auth section) warns against using it for data-API calls; the only remaining production caller is `dispatch/mode_local.go:30` retained as a test seam alias. Rename to `LookupAuthHostToken` (or move to an internal package) so its narrow purpose is obvious from the call site, removing the \"is this safe?\" cognitive load.\n\n#### Medium — Shim's backward-compat fallback is a load-bearing leaky abstraction\n`store.go:68-88,112-129` falls back to `keyring.Get` directly when `tokenstore.Keyring` returns `ErrMalformed`. This *is* the right place for it (entire-specific upgrade path), but the library's `ErrMalformed` exists only to support this one caller. Document that explicitly in `auth/tokenstore/tokenstore.go:18-23` (currently it says \"used by callers that want to treat … as a legacy/upgrade path\" without naming who) so a second CLI doesn't have to reverse-engineer the design.\n\n#### Medium — Test seams `Config.Exchange` / `Config.Now` are correctly scoped\nProduction callers in this repo never set them; they're nil-checked and fall through to real impls (`tokenmanager.go:129-131,349-351`). Good. The `auth.SetManagerForTest` shape (taking `interface{ Helper() }`) avoids dragging `testing.T` into production imports. Keep as-is.\n\n#### Low — `secondsUntil` in shim re-derives `expires_in` only to satisfy the legacy `DeviceAuthPoll.ExpiresIn` field\n`client.go:155-162`. `ExpiresIn` is unused — `runLogin` (`login.go:82-92`) reads `start.ExpiresIn` for the deadline and `result.AccessToken` for the token; it never reads `result.ExpiresIn`. Drop the field and the helper, and remove the `nowFunc` package-level mutable.\n\n#### Low — `client_id` doubles as `UserAgent`\n`exchange.go:60` and `client.go:50-53` set `UserAgent: provider.clientID`. That's `\"entire-cli\"` with no version. The library lets you set anything; pass a real UA like `\"entire-cli/\" + version.Version()` so server-side logs can correlate by build.\n\n#### Low — `auth/doc.go` says \"Entire CLI auth library\" but README says \"shareable across CLIs\"\n`auth/doc.go:1` calls it \"the umbrella for the Entire CLI auth library.\" README sells it as multi-tenant. Pick one framing — probably the README's, since the design has clearly been done for it.\n\n### 4. Forward-Compat Risks for a Second CLI\n\n1. **`tokenmanager.Manager` is a value-typed `Config` constructor — good.** A second CLI imports `auth/tokenmanager` and `auth/tokenstore` and is done.\n2. **No retry / refresh-token policy in the manager.** `TokenSet.RefreshToken` is captured (`tokens/tokens.go:26`) but `tokenmanager` never uses it. First CLI to need refresh will have to add it; design the hook now (a `Config.OnExpired` callback?) or document the omission.\n3. **`Provider` concept lives only in the shim.** A second CLI will rewrite an equivalent table. Consider promoting a tiny `auth/provider` helper struct (clientID + 4 paths) so embedders don't reinvent it — optional, but cheap.\n4. **Singleton in the shim (`managerOnce`)** is fine for one CLI but not pattern-worthy. Document in README that consumers can hold the `*Manager` themselves.\n\n### 5. Recommendations (in priority order)\n\n1. Eliminate the duplicated `ENTIRE_AUTH_PROVIDER_VERSION` read in `cmd/entire/cli/api/auth_tokens.go`.\n2. Read provider version once at startup; pass `Provider` explicitly to `NewClient` and `defaultManager`.\n3. Rename `LookupCurrentToken` → `LookupAuthHostToken` (or move to `internal/`).\n4. Tighten `auth/tokenstore` docs to name the upgrade-path use case for `ErrMalformed`.\n5. Drop `DeviceAuthPoll.ExpiresIn` + `secondsUntil` + `nowFunc` from the shim.\n6. Reconcile `auth/doc.go` framing with `README.md`.\n\n### Files Cited\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/tokenmanager/tokenmanager.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/tokenstore/tokenstore.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/sts/sts.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/tokens/tokens.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/doc.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/auth/README.md`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/auth/provider.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/auth/exchange.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/auth/client.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/auth/store.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/api/auth_tokens.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/api/client.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/api_client.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/login.go`</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>87536</total_tokens><tool_uses>27</tool_uses><duration_ms>119868</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
