{"parentUuid":"63cdaacb-a7f8-4d50-9bea-507ee324d6da","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bf75385c-e02e-41fe-969d-8f953ecf1e1e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jjscdGCodWajwMvxybZ4P","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Package tokenmanager orchestrates core-token storage and RFC 8693\n2\t// token exchanges for an OAuth 2.0 device-flow client.\n3\t//\n4\t// One Manager per CLI process. Construct it once from the embedding\n5\t// CLI's identity (Issuer, ClientID, STSPath, Store) and call\n6\t// TokenForResource / Token from data-API call sites.\n7\t//\n8\t// The package is provider-agnostic: every endpoint, identifier, and\n9\t// default value comes from Config. It has no env-var reads, no\n10\t// implicit URLs, and no embedded provider tables. Tests inject\n11\t// Config.Exchange and Config.Now to avoid hitting the network and to\n12\t// freeze the clock.\n13\tpackage tokenmanager\n14\t\n15\timport (\n16\t\t\"context\"\n17\t\t\"errors\"\n18\t\t\"fmt\"\n19\t\t\"net/http\"\n20\t\t\"net/url\"\n21\t\t\"slices\"\n22\t\t\"strings\"\n23\t\t\"sync\"\n24\t\t\"time\"\n25\t\n26\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/auth/sts\"\n27\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/auth/tokens\"\n28\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/auth/tokenstore\"\n29\t)\n30\t\n31\t// DefaultRequestedTokenType is the RFC 8693 §3 URI used when neither\n32\t// Config.RequestedTokenType nor TokenRequest.RequestedTokenType is set.\n33\t// :access_token is the canonical \"give me an OAuth access token\" URI;\n34\t// the wire format is the server's choice.\n35\t//\n36\t//nolint:gosec // RFC 8693 token-type URI, not a credential\n37\tconst DefaultRequestedTokenType = \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token\"\n38\t\n39\t// exchangeSkew is the safety margin applied when deciding whether a\n40\t// cached exchanged token is still usable. Set conservatively because\n41\t// the worst case (re-exchange one extra time per command) is cheap.\n42\tconst exchangeSkew = 30 * time.Second\n43\t\n44\t// ErrNotLoggedIn is returned by Token / TokenForResource when no core\n45\t// token is present in the store. Callers can match on it to render a\n46\t// \"run <login>\" message.\n47\tvar ErrNotLoggedIn = errors.New(\"not logged in\")\n48\t\n49\t// ErrNoSTSPath is returned when an exchange is needed but Config.STSPath\n50\t// is empty. Single-host deployments hit the same-host shortcut and never\n51\t// reach this; split-host deployments must configure STSPath.\n52\tvar ErrNoSTSPath = errors.New(\"token exchange required but Config.STSPath is empty\")\n53\t\n54\t// Config configures a Manager.\n55\ttype Config struct {\n56\t\t// Issuer is the auth host base URL where the device-flow login\n57\t\t// happened and STS exchanges are POSTed. Required. Doubles as the\n58\t\t// Store profile key, so a user can be logged into multiple issuers\n59\t\t// (e.g. regions / staging) without conflict.\n60\t\tIssuer string\n61\t\n62\t\t// ClientID identifies the public client per RFC 6749 §2.3.1 / §3.2.1.\n63\t\t// Sent on STS exchanges via the client_id form field. Required.\n64\t\tClientID string\n65\t\n66\t\t// STSPath is the path on Issuer where token-exchange requests are\n67\t\t// POSTed. Optional: single-host deployments never trigger an\n68\t\t// exchange (the same-host shortcut wins) so they can leave it\n69\t\t// empty. When empty and an exchange is attempted, runExchange\n70\t\t// returns ErrNoSTSPath rather than POSTing to a bogus URL.\n71\t\tSTSPath string\n72\t\n73\t\t// Store persists the core token. Required. Use any tokenstore.Store\n74\t\t// implementation; a per-CLI service name keeps credentials isolated\n75\t\t// from other CLIs sharing this library.\n76\t\tStore tokenstore.Store\n77\t\n78\t\t// RequestedTokenType is the default RFC 8693 requested_token_type\n79\t\t// URI. Empty → DefaultRequestedTokenType.\n80\t\tRequestedTokenType string\n81\t\n82\t\t// Scope is the default scope sent on exchanges. Empty → omitted.\n83\t\tScope string\n84\t\n85\t\t// UserAgent 